    {
      "v": 7,
      "zh": "但在第七位天使吹号发声的时候，　神的奥秘就成全了，正如　神所传给他仆人众先知的佳音。",
      "en": "But in the days[NOTE:1] when the seventh angel is about to blow his trumpet, the mystery of God is completed,[NOTE:2] just as he has[NOTE:3] proclaimed to his servants[NOTE:4] the prophets.”",
      "notes": [
        "Grk “But in the days of the voice of the seventh angel.”",
        "The aorist ἐτελέσθη (etelesthē) has been translated as a proleptic (futuristic) aorist (ExSyn 564 cites this verse as an example).",
        "The time of the action described by the aorist εὐηγγέλισεν (euēngelisen) seems to be past with respect to the aorist passive ἐτελέσθη (etelesthē). This does not require that the prophets in view here be OT prophets. They may actually refer to the martyrs in the church (so G. B. Caird, Revelation [HNTC], 129).",
        "See the note on the word “servants” in 1:1."
      ],
