      "v": 9,
      "zh": "我就走到天使那里，对他说：「请你把小书卷给我。」他对我说：「你拿着吃尽了，便叫你肚子发苦，然而在你口中要甜如蜜。」",
      "en": "So[NOTE:1] I went to the angel and asked him to give me the little scroll. He[NOTE:2] said to me, “Take the scroll[NOTE:3] and eat it. It[NOTE:4] will make your stomach bitter, but it will be as sweet as honey in your mouth.”",
      "notes": [
        "Here καί (kai) has been translated as “so” to indicate the implied result of the instructions given by the voice.",
